---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Ticker from '../../components/Ticker.astro';
import Portrait from '../../components/Portrait.astro';
import Glyph from '../../components/Glyph.astro';
import Illustration from '../../components/Illustration.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../components/NextSteps.astro';
import { faithIntegratedTherapyService, faqPage } from '../../data/schema';

const tickerItems = ['Meaning', 'Identity', 'Relationships', 'Anxiety', 'Grief', 'Discernment', 'Responsibility', 'Hope'];

const whoThisIsFor = [
  {
    title: 'When you want your life to feel more aligned',
    copy: 'You may be carrying anxiety, habits, relationship patterns, or decisions that do not feel consistent with the life you want to live. You are not looking for someone to tell you what to believe. You want space to understand what is getting in the way and to make changes that feel honest, grounded, and connected to your values.',
  },
  {
    title: 'When a relationship has become difficult',
    copy: 'Something important has shifted in a marriage, family, friendship, or church community. You may feel hurt, disappointed, resentful, or unsure how to speak honestly without losing connection. Together, we can make room for the complexity of love, forgiveness, boundaries, responsibility, and repair.',
  },
  {
    title: 'When faith and real life feel harder to hold together',
    copy: 'You hold your faith deeply while finding that life no longer fits as neatly into the answers you once had. Your questions and wrestling are not a rejection of your faith; they may be an invitation to engage more deeply and honestly with the life you are actually living.',
  },
  {
    title: 'When you are tired of carrying it alone',
    copy: 'You may be in a position of leadership, competent and dependable in the roles you hold, while privately feeling overwhelmed, disconnected, restless, or depressed. Therapy can be a place to bring what has been difficult to talk about without having to minimize it, explain your faith from the beginning, or have everything figured out first.',
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Are you a Christian therapist?',
    a: ['My training includes an M.A. in Spiritual Formation and Soul Care from Talbot School of Theology, so the Christian tradition is familiar territory and you will not need to translate it for me. I work with people across and outside that tradition. What matters clinically is that your spiritual life is real to you and belongs in the room, not that we hold the same positions.'],
  },
  {
    q: 'Will we pray together in session?',
    a: ['No. Some practices do this and it can be meaningful for the right person with the right clinician. It is not part of my work. Prayer inside a therapeutic relationship introduces an authority dynamic into a room where we are often examining exactly that, and I would rather keep the hour clear for a different kind of attention.'],
  },
  {
    q: 'How is this different from spiritual direction?',
    a: ['Spiritual direction attends to your relationship with God and treats that relationship as the subject. Therapy attends to you: your history, your patterns, and the reasons you are the particular person having that relationship in the way you are. Many people find the two work well alongside each other, and I am glad to work with someone who already has a director.'],
  },
  {
    q: 'My faith has gone flat and I do not know if that is a spiritual problem or depression. Which is it?',
    a: ['Sometimes both, and the distinction is worth taking time over rather than settling quickly. Spiritual dryness has a long history in the contemplative tradition and is not in itself a clinical condition. Depression is, and it can also present as a loss of meaning that looks spiritual from the inside. Part of early work is getting a careful look at what is actually going on rather than assuming.'],
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you work with pastors and people in vocational ministry?',
    a: ['Yes. When work, faith, community, and income all sit in the same place, there is often nowhere to say the honest thing. Sessions are confidential and are not shared with your church, your board, or your denomination.'],
  },
  {
    q: 'What if part of my spiritual history is painful rather than sustaining?',
    a: ['That is common and it belongs here too. Faith is rarely all one thing. If the harder material turns out to be the larger part of the picture, you may find the page on <a href="/services/religious-trauma-therapy/">religious trauma therapy</a> is closer to where you are, and either way we can work with both.'],
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you take insurance?',
    a: ['I am a private-pay practice. Many clients use out-of-network benefits through a PPO plan, and I provide a monthly superbill you can submit for reimbursement. I also accept HSA and FSA cards.'],
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Christian & Faith-Integrated Therapy | Newport Beach"
  description="A Christian therapist for anxiety, relationships, grief, and life, with your faith welcome in the room. Newport Beach, Fullerton, and CA telehealth."
  active="/services/"
  path="/services/faith-integrated-therapy/"
  schema={[
    faithIntegratedTherapyService,
    faqPage(faqs, {
      id: 'https://nikolesparks.com/services/faith-integrated-therapy#faq',
      url: 'https://nikolesparks.com/services/faith-integrated-therapy',
    }),
  ]}
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/services/">Services</a> / Christian therapy</p>
      <h1>Your spiritual life is not <em>a separate appointment.</em></h1>
      <p>
        What would it feel like to have your faith understood as part of the whole picture? For
        many people, their faith is the ground from which they understand love, suffering,
        purpose, responsibility, forgiveness, and belonging. It informs the choices they make,
        the relationships they tend, and the life they hope to live. I offer depth-oriented,
        faith-integrated therapy in Newport Beach and Fullerton, and by telehealth throughout
        California.
      </p>
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Schedule a free consultation <span class="arw">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <svg class="hero-figure faith-hero-art" viewBox="0 0 370 370" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Concentric rings expanding from a single point, illustrating a life understood as a whole rather than in separate parts">
      <circle cx="185" cy="185" r="184.375" fill="url(#faith-hero-grad)" stroke="#3B63C4" stroke-width="1"/>
      <path d="M185 306.937C236.062 306.937 282.275 310.5 315.709 316.255C332.431 319.133 345.926 322.555 355.227 326.34C359.879 328.233 363.446 330.204 365.839 332.217C368.237 334.235 369.375 336.222 369.375 338.156C369.375 340.09 368.237 342.078 365.839 344.096C363.446 346.109 359.879 348.078 355.227 349.972C345.926 353.757 332.431 357.179 315.709 360.058C282.275 365.813 236.062 369.375 185 369.375C133.938 369.375 87.7248 365.813 54.291 360.058C37.5691 357.179 24.0737 353.757 14.7734 349.972C10.1209 348.078 6.55413 346.109 4.16113 344.096C1.76265 342.078 0.625182 340.09 0.625 338.156C0.625 336.222 1.7625 334.235 4.16113 332.217C6.55413 330.204 10.1207 328.233 14.7734 326.34C24.0737 322.555 37.5692 319.133 54.291 316.255C87.7248 310.5 133.938 306.937 185 306.937Z" stroke="#3B63C4" stroke-width="1"/>
      <path d="M185 241.731C236.035 241.731 282.213 248.938 315.609 260.572C332.31 266.39 345.781 273.304 355.064 280.95C364.352 288.599 369.375 296.916 369.375 305.553C369.375 314.189 364.352 322.507 355.064 330.156C345.781 337.802 332.31 344.715 315.609 350.533C282.213 362.167 236.035 369.375 185 369.375C133.965 369.375 87.787 362.167 54.3906 350.533C37.6897 344.715 24.2188 337.802 14.9355 330.156C5.64801 322.507 0.625 314.189 0.625 305.553C0.625169 296.916 5.6482 288.599 14.9355 280.95C24.2188 273.304 37.6896 266.39 54.3906 260.572C87.787 248.938 133.965 241.731 185 241.731Z" stroke="#3B63C4" stroke-width="1"/>
      <path d="M185 182.592C236.009 182.592 282.158 193.1 315.531 210.061C348.94 227.039 369.375 250.38 369.375 275.983C369.375 301.586 348.939 324.927 315.531 341.905C282.158 358.866 236.009 369.375 185 369.375C133.991 369.375 87.8424 358.866 54.4688 341.905C21.0606 324.927 0.62511 301.586 0.625 275.983C0.625 250.38 21.0605 227.039 54.4688 210.061C87.8424 193.1 133.991 182.592 185 182.592Z" stroke="#3B63C4" stroke-width="1"/>
      <path d="M185 124.97C235.981 124.97 282.106 138.69 315.469 160.841C348.836 182.994 369.375 213.53 369.375 247.173C369.375 280.816 348.836 311.35 315.469 333.504C282.106 355.654 235.981 369.375 185 369.375C134.019 369.375 87.8937 355.654 54.5312 333.504C21.1643 311.35 0.625106 280.816 0.625 247.173C0.625 213.53 21.1642 182.994 54.5312 160.841C87.8936 138.69 134.019 124.97 185 124.97Z" stroke="#3B63C4" stroke-width="1"/>
      <path d="M185 67.3467C286.949 67.3467 369.375 135.069 369.375 218.361C369.375 301.654 286.949 369.375 185 369.375C83.0507 369.375 0.625201 301.654 0.625 218.361C0.625 135.069 83.0505 67.3467 185 67.3467Z" stroke="#3B63C4" stroke-width="1"/>
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="faith-hero-grad" x1="184.397" y1="319.574" x2="184.396" y2="23.3835" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <stop stop-color="#C7D64F"/>
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#C7D64F" stop-opacity="0"/>
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>
    </svg>
  </section>

  <Ticker items={tickerItems} label="Where faith and life meet" />

  <!-- The premise -->
  <section class="section split c-wide-narrow" style="align-items:center">
    <div class="col gap-28">
      <p class="eyebrow">The premise</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif h2-lg">An invitation to bring <em>your faith</em> into the room.</h2>
      <p class="body">There are parts of life that are hard to put into words: the strain in a relationship, the anger underneath grief, the uncertainty that lingers after a decision, the guilt that surfaces without a clear cause, the longing to feel more connected to yourself and the people you love.</p>
      <p class="body">When faith is part of how you understand your life, these experiences rarely stay separate from it. Questions of responsibility, forgiveness, hope, desire, loss, and belonging are woven through your spiritual life, not set apart from it. So when you invite someone in to help, it matters that they can understand the values and the worldview your life is built on.</p>
      <p class="body">Therapy can be a place to look at these things with someone who respects and understands what shapes them. You do not have to make your faith the focus of every conversation, and you do not have to leave it at the door. Together, we can linger with what hurts, what matters, and what is asking to be understood more deeply.</p>
    </div>
    <Illustration name="integration-full" size="clamp(340px, 38vw, 480px)" color="var(--blue)" class="hero-figure premise-figure" />
  </section>

  <!-- Who this is for -->
  <section class="section sage on-color">
    <div class="stack gap-20" style="margin-bottom:48px">
      <p class="eyebrow on-color">Who I work with</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif" style="max-width:760px">For people whose faith is <em>integral to their life and story.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="process-grid cols-2">
      {whoThisIsFor.map((c, i) => (
        <div class="process-card">
          <span class="num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <div class="title">{c.title}</div>
          <p>{c.copy}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What the work looks like -->
  <section class="section split c-narrow-wide">
    <div class="col gap-20">
      <p class="eyebrow">The work</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif"><em>Attention,</em> not advice.</h2>
      <svg class="work-figure" viewBox="0 0 263 280" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="A network of linked circles radiating from a central point, suggesting how separate parts of a life connect">
        <circle cx="107.559" cy="130.08" r="63.9172" transform="rotate(180 107.559 130.08)" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <circle cx="38" cy="242" r="37.5" transform="rotate(180 38 242)" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <circle cx="119" cy="38" r="37.5" transform="rotate(180 119 38)" fill="url(#paint0_linear_91_508)" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <circle cx="243" cy="132" r="19.5" transform="rotate(180 243 132)" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <circle cx="48" cy="132" r="19.5" transform="rotate(180 48 132)" fill="url(#paint1_linear_91_508)" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <circle cx="155" cy="212" r="19.5" transform="rotate(180 155 212)" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <line x1="58.5713" y1="210.743" x2="107.132" y2="129.822" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <line x1="107.058" y1="130.022" x2="113.503" y2="74.9424" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <line x1="67.0703" y1="131.42" x2="223.512" y2="131.42" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <line x1="145.782" y1="194.754" x2="107.132" y2="130.337" stroke="#3B63C4"/>
        <circle cx="107" cy="131" r="8" transform="rotate(180 107 131)" fill="#C7D64F"/>
        <defs>
          <linearGradient id="paint0_linear_91_508" x1="124.5" y1="1.5" x2="123.5" y2="8" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <stop stop-color="#C7D64F"/>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#C7D64F" stop-opacity="0"/>
          </linearGradient>
          <linearGradient id="paint1_linear_91_508" x1="52.5" y1="132" x2="32.6154" y2="132" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <stop stop-color="#C7D64F" stop-opacity="0"/>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#C7D64F"/>
          </linearGradient>
        </defs>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="prose prose-15">
      <p class="body">There are some questions no one else can answer for you. Questions of love, responsibility, loss, calling, and what faithfulness asks in a particular season of life are not solved by receiving the right advice. Therapy can offer another kind of space: one where we slow down enough to notice what is happening beneath the surface. Your faith is invited and present in the room because it is already part of how you make meaning, carry responsibility, and imagine a way forward.</p>
      <p class="body">Often, the work begins with something small. A resentment you have brushed aside. A fear that appears whenever you disappoint someone. A recurring sense of obligation, or the realization that it has become difficult to tell the difference between love, fear, guilt, and duty. Sometimes it means looking more closely at a relationship, a decision, a sense of loneliness, or a role you have held for so long that you no longer know where it ends and you begin.</p>
      <p class="body">Depth work does not rush toward a conclusion. It gives us time to understand what is beneath the first explanation. As we do, distinctions often become clearer: between generosity and overextension, anxiety that confirms what you already fear and the fear that can arise when healing asks something new of you, love and obligation, forgiveness and avoiding what is painful to face.</p>
      <p class="body">The hope is not that therapy will provide certainty where life does not. It is that, through careful attention, you may become freer to discern, to love, to receive your own life more honestly, and to respond with greater sturdiness and integrity to what is in front of you.</p>
      <p class="body">More on <a href="/approach/" style="color:var(--blue); border-bottom:1px solid var(--blue)">how I work</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Therapy and spiritual direction -->
  <section class="section ink on-color split c-wide-narrow">
    <div class="col gap-28">
      <p class="eyebrow on-color">A helpful distinction</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif">Therapy can include faith<br><em>without becoming spiritual direction.</em></h2>
      <p class="body">Your relationship with God is connected to your history, relationships, longings, losses, and hopes. In therapy, we can attend to how these parts of your life meet, without reducing faith to psychology or turning therapy into a place for advice.</p>
      <p class="body">Spiritual direction has a different focus: your relationship with God and the movement of your spiritual life. Therapy focuses on you: your story, emotions, relationships, and the patterns that shape how you experience your life and what feels possible. I am trained in both areas and hold a master’s degree in Spiritual Formation and Soul Care from Talbot School of Theology, and if spiritual direction would be helpful alongside therapy, I can connect you with a trusted referral.</p>
    </div>
    <Glyph name="nested-ellipses" class="hero-figure" />
  </section>

  <!-- Background -->
  <section class="section split c-media">
    <Portrait src="/nikole_sparks-mft-website.jpg" alt="Nikole Sparks" placeholder="Nikole — candid photo" />
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">Background</p>
      <h2 class="serif h2-lg">You should not have to <em class="accent">leave<br>faith outside the room.</em></h2>
      <p class="body">You’re probably on this page because faith is not an add-on to the rest of life. It shapes how you understand love, calling, suffering, responsibility, hope, and what it means to become more fully yourself. I bring an MA in Spiritual Formation and Soul Care from Talbot School of Theology, as well as training in spiritual direction. That background means your faith and values do not have to be translated or defended in order to be taken seriously.</p>
      <p class="body">I also bring a depth-oriented clinical approach, informed by ongoing postgraduate psychoanalytic training at the Newport Psychoanalytic Institute. That combination allows me to meet the spiritual and psychological dimensions of your life without positioning one versus the other. We can speak openly about faith, prayer, calling, doubt, suffering, relationships, and the patterns that shape how you experience them.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/about/">About Nikole <span class="arw">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQs -->
  <section class="section" style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1.5fr; gap:80px; align-items:start">
    <div class="sticky-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Faith-integrated therapy</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <Illustration name="questions-full" size="240px" class="mt-16" />
    </div>
    <Faq items={faqs} />
  </section>

  <!-- The bridge to religious trauma therapy -->
  <section class="section sage on-color">
    <div class="stack gap-20" style="max-width:760px">
      <p class="eyebrow on-color">A companion path</p>
      <h2 class="h2-serif">If what you are carrying is <em>heavier than this.</em></h2>
      <p class="body">Faith is rarely all one thing. Some of what you were given sustains you and some of it may have cost you something, and those can be true in the same person on the same Sunday.</p>
      <p class="body">If the harder part is the larger part right now, <a href="/services/religious-trauma-therapy/" style="color:var(--cream); border-bottom:1px solid var(--cream-35)">therapy for religious trauma</a> is where that work is described. It is the same practice and the same clinician. You do not need to have sorted out which page you belong on before you call, and most people do not arrive knowing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextSteps
    heading="Bring the whole thing. <em>Let’s talk.</em>"
    copy="The free 15-minute consultation is a conversation, not an intake. In-person in Newport Beach and Fullerton, or telehealth throughout California."
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Size the custom hero SVG by width and center it in the hero column,
     overriding the generic .hero-figure { width:100% } used by inline art. */
  svg.faith-hero-art {
    width: clamp(300px, 40vw, 460px);
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: block;
  }
  /* Center the premise illustration within its narrow column so it sits
     balanced rather than hugging the left edge. */
  .premise-figure {
    justify-self: center;
    align-self: start;
  }
  /* Small linked-circles figure under the short "The work" heading, filling
     the empty space in the narrow column. */
  .work-figure {
    width: clamp(200px, 22vw, 250px);
    height: auto;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    section[style*='grid-template-columns:1fr 1.5fr'] {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
      gap: 40px !important;
    }
  }
</style>
